e and the approximate double bottom with 2357.18, weakening the Always-In Long read and supporting a larger trading range 2357.18-2850.", "Range development: five or more further bars overlapping inside 2633.31-2786.81 without a new high would turn the pause into a trading range at the highs and lower Always-In relevance."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790395199999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["Since the 2850 high the sequence is lower highs (2804.59, 2786.81, 2740.42) and lower lows (2648.49, 2633.31), and the highest close in that stretch is 2775.61, so the bull leg has not re-asserted.", "The final close 2686.84 is below the 2633.31-2804.59 midpoint of 2718.95, and the last 11 closes sit in the lower half of the post-spike range.", "The same window contains a decline from 2609.02 to 2358.62 with large bear bars closing at 2423.29 and 2412.95, so the trend label is window-dependent and a bear resumption is not excluded.", "Spike highs here have not been durable: the 2850 bar left a 126.85 upper tail, and the earlier 2680 spike was fully retraced to 2358.62 within 25 bars."], "evidence_for": ["Higher highs and higher lows dominate the last 63 bars: 2358.62 (bar open_time 1789502400000), pullback lows 2568.16 and 2716.01, then 2850; the post-spike low 2633.31 still sits far above 2358.62.", "Bull breakout with follow-through: bars open_time 1789732800000 and 1789747200000 closed at 2578.6 and 2636.28 near their highs, and no close since has returned below the 2495.82 breakout-bar low.", "Bear attempts after the 2850 high lack acceptance: bear closes at 2586.68 (bar open_time 1789848000000), 2659 (bar open_time 1790164800000) and 2647.9 (bar open_time 1790236800000) were each followed by higher closes (2611, 2676.47, 2682.25).", "Recent price action is two-sided and overlapping between